## Extract values from the graph.
Values for each bar is written at the top of each bar. Hence:
Population Growth for Vulcan States is 20,000,000 and for Non-Vulcan States, 5,000,000;
Employment Growth for Vulcan States is 10,000,000 and for Non-Vulcan States, 6,000,000;
Household Growth for Vulcan States is 11,000,000 and for Non-Vulcan States, 4,000,000.
This is found labeled on each one of the 6 bars in the bar graph.

## Calculate the differences in growths between Vulcan States and Non-Vulcan States for each demographic growth.
For each demographic growth, compute Vulcan States Growth - Non-Vulcan States Growth, leading to:
Vulcan vs Non-Vulcan Population Growths difference = 20,000,000 - 5,000,000 = 15,000,000;
Vulcan vs Non-Vulcan Employment Growths difference = 10,000,000 - 6,000,000 = 4,000,000;
Vulcan vs Non-Vulcan Household Growths difference = 11,000,000 - 4,000,000 = 7,000,000.

